        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Places: Bolling–Gatewood House\n- People: Ida B. Wells\n- Organizations: Ida B. Wells-Barnett Museum, National Association for the Advancement of Colored People (NAACP)\n- Roles: journalist, suffragist, founder, former slave\n\nFacts:\n- In 1909, Ida B. Wells was one of the founders of the National Association for the Advancement of Colored People (NAACP).\n- The Bolling–Gatewood House is home to the Ida B. Wells-Barnett Museum.\n- The Ida B. Wells-Barnett Museum is named for Ida B. Wells, who was a former slave, journalist, and suffragist.",
